# Unit Testing

The `unit/` directory contains tests used to verify individual software components of the AutoLink RadioSense system in isolation.

Unit tests focus on the correctness of specific functions, classes, algorithms, and software modules without requiring the complete system or physical communication between hardware devices.

## Purpose

The purpose of unit testing is to identify and verify the correctness of individual software components before they are integrated into the complete system.

Typical unit tests may include:

* Testing individual functions and classes
* Verifying data validation and processing logic
* Testing packet parsing and field extraction
* Testing RSSI, SNR, and PDR calculations
* Testing geographic distance and progress calculations
* Testing relay-selection and routing calculations
* Verifying boundary conditions and invalid inputs
* Detecting software defects at an early stage of development

## Organization

Unit tests are organized according to the software subsystem or functionality being tested.

```text
unit/
├── README.md
├── Beacon/
├── Neighbour/
├── LinkQuality/
└── Routing/
```

Additional test directories may be added as new software modules are developed.

## Testing Approach

Each unit test should focus on a specific software component and should minimize dependencies on other components or physical hardware.

Where possible, tests should use predefined inputs and expected outputs so that the correctness of the tested component can be determined objectively.

## Scope

Unit testing is primarily concerned with **software-level verification**. It does not replace system-level testing using the actual ESP32 and LoRa hardware.

The results of unit testing should be used together with system-level testing to verify the overall reliability of the AutoLink RadioSense system.
